ns or go do other things and take  on a world boss or a local event so you  have choice there and then you have pve  versus pvp so do you want to go and take  on the story you know campaign content  or do you want to go and fight other  players in one of our sort of pvp areas  and then who do you want to play with is  a choice right you can play so it's a  great game solo but you can party up  everything along the way is really about  what you decide you want to do and so  that's what why we talk about d4s about  choice is because pretty much every step  along the process there's some things  that you have agency over and you can  decide how you want to play the game  all of the classes in diablo 4 have this  sort of unique feature that's unique to  just that class and the necromancer is  the book of the dead where you decide oh  i can have skeleton warriors what kind  of skeleton wars do i want do i want  aggressive defensive do i ones that  create corpses for me to use as sort of  raw materials and then oh you can have  mages okay what kind of mages do i want  to use and oh i can have gollum what  kind of golem do i want to use and so  you can mix and match your warriors your  mages and your golem to really create  and customize the army that you have  with you and you never really had that  experience before  and that's what really is one of the  things that makes the new necro really  unique and interesting i like to talk  about diablo 4 being the culmination of  the franchise because it wants to  respect the past like there's and so  when you look at  kind of what goes into diablo 4 i like  to use the formula that it feels like  it's the dark tone of diablo 1.  it's the progression of diablo ii it's  the the visceral combat of diablo iii  and then it has  its own unique innovations in diablo 4  with the shared open world and all the  things we talked about with player  choice i think there are ways there are  lots of ways that we've looked at  lessons learned from previous games too  you know one of the great innovations we  made with legendary items and again  speaking to that idea of having multiple  builds available is that you can take  legendary power off  an item and move it to  another item so it really opens up the  ability to customize your gear we don't  talk about that enough you know in  previous thing games like you would pick  up a shield that have this thing that  would make i can now summon two more  skeleton mages and you're like oh i have  to keep this for as long as pop my build  knees those two extra mages and  eventually your level would outpace it  and you're like  like i don't want to give up the shield  i'm going to carry this shield even  though it's weak because i want this  ability and now in diablo 4 you can  actually extract that off the shield get  a new legendary that's at your level and  put that onto it and so that idea of  being able to hold on to your build and  be able to truly customize your  character by taking legendary powers and  distracting them from one thing and  imbuing them into another that  fundamentally changes the build system  so one of the things that's really  exciting about diablo 4 is that because  we have the shared open world that  exists as a template the dungeons are  actually in places in the world that  you're going to explore and those to  give those gives those dungeons a real  sense of um of place  so when you go into a particular dungeon  you're going to see  the tile set that's associated with that  dungeon that that type of art we have a  wide variety of  art  for these  and you're also going to see the  monsters that live in it but when the  dungeon  rolls  it is randomly generated within those  parameters the monsters will be  differently configured you're going to  see different champions you're going to  see different affixes  and you're going to see a different  layout for that dungeon on top of that  each dungeon has a dungeon objective  so when you go in you might have an  objective to slay a boss but you might  have an objective to  track down three fallen idols and  disable them and so the completion  objective for the dungeon uh is is  unique to each dungeon as well and one  of the things i really like when we play  is that you go in and you don't know the  objective like there's not some magical  person at the door telling you by the  way the reason how you complete this is  like you have to go in and discover the  objective which is really fun and the  dungeons actually play really well into  our end game right where you now not  only do you have the dungeons that  you're doing when you're playing through  the campaign regularly for say new gear  or a particular thing but  at the end all of a sudden you have  nightmare dungeons where did you want to  talk a little bit about like the sigils  and that you can upgrade the dungeons  with these sigils to make them nightmare  dungeons and they become more dangerous  additional affixes are applied to them  that make the monsters more dangerous or  can even um give you advantages  um and when you're uh getting these  sigils you'll get a wide variety of  sigils with all kinds of different  affixes on them so there's once again  player choice in which sigils you want  to do and if you get a sigil that uh is  for a dungeon that you know is not as  you don't think is well suited to your  class you just skip that one in two  different ones nightmare dungeons is  sort of our take on riffs and so if  you've played the previous diablo 3  there would be there's you know a thing  in town and you just go to it and opens  a portal and off you go and you're  standing in town  going to it over and over  and now we have these nightmare dungeons  which is kind of like running a rift in  a way but it has a sense of place so now  you have keys and so joe has sigils i  have sigils we're like okay where do we  want to go like we have to go somewhere  now and like okay let's mount up get on  our horses and we're going to ride west  and because that dungeon has a  particular type of loot that we want to  have our type of gear that we want to  get  and so i love that feeling of place and  not just grabbing a portal in town every  time we know that  it's fun to build your character and  discover all these powerful builds  and we also think it's really important  to have content to test that test  yourself against so we've really tried  to expand the  the variety of activities and you know  as rod said the the game um you know  when you finish the campaign you might  be level 45 or something your character  level goes up to 100 through uh through  paragon points and you get access to uh  to whispers you get access to nightmare  dungeons  other endgame activities that that we're  still working on  we really wanted you to have a wide  variety of things to do and of course  you've got  you've got world tiers that are allowing  you to step up the keep have make sure  that the difficulty of the world stays  on pace with the power of your character  level  and to unlock those um you actually need  to  uh to prove to complete a dungeon to to  access that more difficult content so it  goes back to the idea of making a build  making it powerful and then testing  yourself against some challenge and the  and the paragon point like so a paragon  system if you play d3 you know the  paragon system in diablo 3 but it was  just basically sliders and on a couple  of different aspects of your character  in diablo 4 paragon is an actual board  that think of it as a  checker board it's much more granular  than that but for simplicity sake i'll  say a checkerboard and you have to  navigate your way by sort of unlocking  squares as you move across the board and  each of those squares is could be plus  five strength or a different ability or  something that enhances your skills and  so you're able to click these different  boards together and make your own path  through 